  (RUNTIME-EXCEPTION.md).
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  flecs.pcpp - the flecs unit: `import flecs;` organizes a program's data as
  entities, components and systems with flecs
  (https://github.com/SanderMertens/flecs), an entity component system with a
  C99 core and a C++ API. A self-describing vendor module: it owns every
  include path, library path, define and link library it needs, per official
  target. The library is libflecs_static.a (one per target), built by
  PaskalCPP-Libs' build-flecs.cmd from flecs' own CMake project (the static
  target, every addon at upstream's defaults), shipped under flecs' MIT
  license. The unit defines flecs_STATIC for every importer (without it
  flecs.h marks the API dllimport on Windows). On Windows it links wsock32,
  ws2_32 (the REST addon's sockets) and dbghelp; on Linux pthread.

  The API is flecs' C++ API as it ships (namespace flecs), called straight
  from PaskalCPP:
  - The world: a `var LWorld: flecs::world;` holds every entity and
    component; it is created by its declaration and freed (with everything
    in it) when it goes out of scope.
  - Components: any PaskalCPP record is a component. A component is
    registered the first time it is used; LWorld.component<T>() registers it
    up front and gives its entity (its .id() is nonzero).
  - Entities: LWorld.entity() makes one, LWorld.entity("Name") makes a named
    one (LWorld.lookup("Name") finds it again). LE.set(LValue) adds or
    replaces a component value, LE.get<T>() reads it (the entity must have
    it), LE.try_get<T>() gives a pointer, nil when the entity lacks it.
    LE.has<T>(), LE.remove<T>(), LE.destruct() and LE.is_alive() do what
    they say.
  - Queries: LWorld.query<A, B>() matches every entity that has all of the
    listed components; .count() is how many match, .each(R) calls R once per
    match.
  - Systems: LWorld.system<A, B>("Name").each(R) registers R to run once per
    matching entity on every LWorld.progress(ADeltaTime) (true while the
    world has not been told to quit; ADeltaTime 0 measures the time itself).
  - Callbacks for .each are ordinary routines, one parameter per listed
    component in the same order: `var` for a component the routine writes,
    `const` for one it only reads (`routine Move(var AP: Position; const AV:
    Velocity);`). A first parameter `const AE: flecs::entity` also receives
    the entity being visited.
==============================================================================*/

module unit flecs;

// Self-describing vendor module: it owns every path it needs.

@addincludepath "$P:res/libs/vendor/flecs/include";

@ifdef TARGET_X86_64_WINDOWS_GNU
  @addlibrarypath "$P:res/libs/vendor/flecs/lib/x86_64-windows-gnu";
@elseif TARGET_X86_64_LINUX_GNU
  @addlibrarypath "$P:res/libs/vendor/flecs/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu";
@else
  @message error "flecs: unsupported target";
@endif

// Static library: flecs.h selects dllimport unless this is defined
@cppdefine "flecs_STATIC";

@linklibrary "flecs_static";

@ifdef TARGET_X86_64_WINDOWS_GNU
  @linklibrary "wsock32";
  @linklibrary "ws2_32";
  @linklibrary "dbghelp";
@elseif TARGET_X86_64_LINUX_GNU
  @linklibrary "pthread";
@endif

// The header goes to this unit's header, so every importer sees flecs' API
cpp header;

#include "flecs.h"

end.
